[[2047,127,0,"<aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Follow the safety instructions\n(\n                                                         <a href=\"#/3238304\">5040A</a>\n                                                          ).</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside>"],[894,127,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Place the vehicle on a lift.</p><p>Drain the coolant. \n                                          <a href=\"#/3238305\">5040A10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238952\">7055A43</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238951\">7055A41</a>\n                                           (right and\nleft)</p><p><a href=\"#/3238959\">7055B10</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolts.</p><p>2. Disconnect the pipe connectors.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Seal the disconnected connectors,\nusing suitable plugs, to prevent humidity and impurities from entering\nthe system.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>3. Undo the bolts.</p><p>4. Remove the duct</p><p>5. Undo the bolts.</p><p>6. Remove the condenser.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018456.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[894,127,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the condenser is intact and\nis not damaged and does not have deposits of dirt on the finned\nsurface.</p><p>Reposition the condenser.</p><p>Tighten the bolt to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>Condenser pipe connector</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>0.4 - 0.5</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Fit the duct securing it using the bolts.</p><p>Connect the pipe connectors.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Replace the O-rings for the connectors.</p><p>Only\nuse green coloured seals, resistant to R134A coolant fluid.</p><p>Lubricate\nthe thread of the connectors using anti-freeze.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Tighten the bolt to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>Condenser pipe connector</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>0.9 - 1.2</p></td></tr></table></div><p><a href=\"#/3238959\">7055B10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238951\">7055A41</a>\n                                           (right and\nleft)</p><p><a href=\"#/3238952\">7055A43</a></p><p>Repressurize using coolant. \n                                          <a href=\"#/3238305\">5040A10</a></p><p>Remove the vehicle from the lift.</p>"],[2047,127,0,"<aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Follow the safety instructions\n(\n                                                         <a href=\"#/3238304\">5040A</a>\n                                                          ).</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside>"],[894,96,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Place the vehicle on a lift.</p><p>Drain the coolant. \n                                          <a href=\"#/3238305\">5040A10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238952\">7055A43</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238951\">7055A41</a>\n                                           (right and\nleft)</p><p><a href=\"#/3238959\">7055B10</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolts.</p><p>2. Disconnect the pipe connectors.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Seal the disconnected connectors,\nusing suitable plugs, to prevent humidity and impurities from entering\nthe system.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>3. Undo the bolts.</p><p>4. Remove the duct</p><p>5. Undo the bolts.</p><p>6. Remove the condenser.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018457.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[894,96,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the condenser is intact and\nis not damaged and does not have deposits of dirt on the finned\nsurface.</p><p>Reposition the condenser.</p><p>Tighten the bolt to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>Condenser pipe connector</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>0.4 - 0.5</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Fit the duct securing it using the bolts.</p><p>Connect the pipe connectors.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Replace the O-rings for the connectors.</p><p>Only\nuse green coloured seals, resistant to R134A coolant fluid.</p><p>Lubricate\nthe thread of the connectors using anti-freeze.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Tighten the bolt to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>Condenser pipe connector</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>0.9</p></td></tr></table></div><p><a href=\"#/3238959\">7055B10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238951\">7055A41</a>\n                                           (right and\nleft)</p><p><a href=\"#/3238952\">7055A43</a></p><p>Repressurize using coolant. \n                                          <a href=\"#/3238305\">5040A10</a></p><p>Remove the vehicle from the lift.</p>"],[128,127,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Observe the following precaution.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Follow the recommended safety\ninstructions (see subgroup 5040 - AIR CONDITIONER CASING AND COMPONENTS)</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p><a href=\"#/3238721\">7025A12</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238722\">7025A14</a></p><p>Drain the coolant (\n                                          <a href=\"#/3238305\">5040A10</a>\n                                           ).</p><p><a href=\"#/3238952\">7055A43</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238951\">7055A41</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3239044\">7210E10</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolt.</p><p>2. Move the power steering fluid cooling pipes to one side.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2070038.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[128,127,16,"<p>1. Undo the bolts.</p><p>2. Disconnect the pipe connectors.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Seal the disconnected connectors,\nusing suitable plugs, to prevent humidity and impurities from entering\nthe system.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>3. Undo the bolts.</p><p>4. Remove the duct</p><p>5. Undo the bolts.</p><p>6. Remove the condenser.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2070039.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[128,127,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the condenser is intact and\nis not damaged and does not have deposits of dirt on the finned\nsurface.</p><p>Position the condenser in its seat.</p><p>Tighten the condenser fixing bolts.</p><p>Fit the duct and secure with bolts.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Replace the O-rings for the connectors.\nOnly use green coloured seals, resistant to R134A refrigerant. Lubricate\nthe thread of the connectors using anti-freeze.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Connect the connectors for the climate\ncontrol system pipes and tighten the bolts.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COOLANT SYSTEM FITTINGS</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>0.9</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Place the power assisted steering fluid\ncooling pipe in position and secure it using the bolt.</p><p><a href=\"#/3239044\">7210E10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238951\">7055A41</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238952\">7055A43</a></p><p>Repressurize using coolant fluid (\n                                          <a href=\"#/3238305\">5040A10</a>\n                                           ).</p><p><a href=\"#/3238722\">7025A14</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238721\">7025A12</a></p>"],[1024,127,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Observe the following precaution.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Follow the recommended safety\ninstructions (see subgroup 5040 - AIR CONDITIONER CASING AND COMPONENTS)</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Drain the coolant (\n                                          <a href=\"#/3238305\">5040A10</a>\n                                           ).</p><p><a href=\"#/3238964\">7055B42</a>\n                                           (left and right)</p><p><a href=\"#/3238951\">7055A41</a>\n                                           (left\nand right)</p><p><a href=\"#/3239044\">7210E10</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolt.</p><p>2. Move the power steering fluid cooling pipes to one side.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2070040.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1024,127,16,"<p>1. Undo the bolts.</p><p>2. Disconnect the pipe connectors.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Seal the disconnected connectors,\nusing suitable plugs, to prevent humidity and impurities from entering\nthe system.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>3. Undo the bolts.</p><p>4. Remove the duct</p><p>5. Undo the bolts.</p><p>6. Remove the condenser.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2070041.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1024,127,16,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the condenser is intact and\nis not damaged and does not have deposits of dirt on the finned\nsurface.</p><p>Position the condenser in its seat.</p><p>Tighten the condenser fixing bolts.</p><p>Fit the duct and secure with bolts.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Replace the O-rings for the connectors.\nOnly use green coloured seals, resistant to R134A refrigerant. Lubricate\nthe thread of the connectors using anti-freeze.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Connect the connectors for the climate\ncontrol system pipes and tighten the bolts.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COOLANT SYSTEM FITTINGS</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>0.9</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Place the power assisted steering fluid\ncooling pipe in position and secure it using the bolt.</p><p><a href=\"#/3239044\">7210E10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238951\">7055A41</a>\n                                           (left\nand right)</p><p><a href=\"#/3238964\">7055B42</a>\n                                           (left and right)</p><p>Repressurize using coolant fluid (\n                                          <a href=\"#/3238305\">5040A10</a>\n                                           ).</p>"]]